Rule 3 (no overflow of narrowed slice for start as int, handling negative dim and negative start)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : int, v_3 : int, v_4 : int} |= if v_2 ≥ 0 then if v_3 ≥ 0 then (v_3 + v_4 ≤ shape(v_1, v_2)) else ((0 - shape(v_1, v_2)) ≤ v_3 ∧ v_3 < 0 ∧ v_4 ≤ (0 - v_3)) else if v_3 ≥ 0 then (v_3 + v_4 ≤ shape(v_1, ndim(v_1) + v_2)) else ((0 - shape(v_1, ndim(v_1) + v_2)) ≤ v_3 ∧ v_3 < 0 ∧ v_4 ≤ (0 - v_3))
>>
Rule 4 (zero-size dimension implies start=0 and length=0 for start as int)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : int, v_3 : int, v_4 : int} |= if v_2 ≥ 0 then if shape(v_1, v_2) = 0 then (v_4 = 0 ∧ v_3 = 0) else if shape(v_1, ndim(v_1) + v_2) = 0 then (v_4 = 0 ∧ v_3 = 0)
